        "titulo": "The master table of adjectives and 20 complete adjectives",
        "explicacao": "The master table of adjectives. Here is the table that solves everything. Notice the beauty of the system: A feminine noun ends in -А/-Я — and the feminine adjective ends in -АЯ/-ЯЯ. A neuter noun ends in -О/-Е — and the neuter adjective ends in -ОЕ/-ЕЕ. A plural noun ends in -Ы/-И — and the plural adjective ends in -ЫЕ/-ИЕ. The system talks to itself. The adjective is a mirror of the noun. If you know the gender of the noun, the adjective fits automatically. That is why lesson 11 (gender of the noun) came before this one. The living table: 20 complete adjectives. Here is the living table. Notice the root of each one. Notice the ending. Notice that the root never changes. Important observations: • 1. The root is always the same. НОВ-, СТАР-, БОЛЬШ-, МАЛЕНЬК-, ХОРОШ-, ПЛОХ-, КРАСИВ-, РУССК-, СИН-, ХОЛОДН-, ГОРЯЧ-, ДОРОГ-, ДЕШЁВ-, МОЛОД-, УМН-, ВКУСН-, СЛАДК-, БЕЛ-, ЧЁРН-. • 2. The ending changes according to the gender. And you only need to memorise the masculine. • 3. Mind the stress. In большо́й and дорого́й the stress is always on the ending (больша́я, большо́е, больши́е; дорога́я, дорого́е, дороги́е). In у́мный it is always on the stem (у́мная, у́мное, у́мные). This does not change the ending, but it changes the pronunciation.",
